         <div type="bio">
            <p>English-German translator and publisher, a leader in the development of the modern paperback edition. He founded the Albatross Press, which published <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Dubliners</name> in 1932. Under an imprint of Albatross, the Odyssey Press, he published <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Ulysses</name>, also in 1932. In 1934 Holroyd-Reece took over the long-established German publisher Tauchnitz, which in 1930 had published a “continental” edition of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
